---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PlatformInstallSelector from '../components/PlatformInstallSelector.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';
import { url } from '../lib/url';
---
<BaseLayout title="Download" description="Install the Inventatory public beta on Windows x64 or Ubuntu Linux x86-64 with verified release packages.">
  <div class="wrap">
    <header class="page-intro"><h1>Download Inventatory</h1><p class="lead">Choose Windows or Ubuntu Linux to see the matching installer. Inventatory keeps your inventory on your own computer, and a scanner is optional.</p></header>
    <PlatformInstallSelector id="download-platforms" />
    <div class="download-notes section">
      <section><h2>Already installed?</h2><p>Use <strong>Settings → Updates</strong> in Inventatory. The updater shows release notes, downloads the package, verifies its published hashes, and hands off to the installer.</p><a href={url('/docs/desktop/settings/#software-updates')}>Read about application updates →</a></section>
      <section><h2>Scanner resources</h2><p>A public Scan R1 firmware release and assembly package have not been verified. Use the scanner documentation to understand the existing desktop integration and its setup requirements.</p><a href={url('/docs/scanner/status/')}>Hardware and firmware status →</a></section>
      <section><h2>Source code and license</h2><p>The desktop application is published under GPL-3.0-only. Build instructions and developer documentation live with the source.</p><a href={site.repository}>Open the application repository ↗</a></section>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
<style>
  .download-notes { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); gap: var(--space-8); padding-top: var(--space-8); border-top: var(--border) solid var(--divider); }
  .download-notes h2 { font-size: var(--text-lead); margin-bottom: var(--space-4); }
  .download-notes a { display: inline-block; margin-top: var(--space-4); }
  @media (max-width: 48rem) { .download-notes { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: var(--space-8); } }
</style>
